# Finite integer search qualification tool

This source-only candidate profiles the actual public route_admitted call against batch27-routing-search. Admission, fixtures, canonical token checks and snapshots precede counters/timing; search consumes the original token, callback and spent guard once. Successful outputs are checked independently for canonical borrowed IDs, exact anchors, orthogonality, open-rectangle clearance and collapsed collinearity after measurement.

The fixed job records ten unchanged-default groups (32/64/128/256/1024 nodes, densities 1/2), each with two warmups and seven measurements. Admission Work/Nodes refusals explicitly have search_called=false and null search metrics. Four separate controls cover default Grid refusal, lowered-to-already-spent work quota, pre-call cancellation and cancellation on search poll 3 after axis reservation. Five malformed CLI cases require exit 2. Wrong outcomes, OOM and timeouts remain failures; there is no fallback or default-limit relaxation.

The allocator is an immutable source dependency from #183 commit 337433fb18a377e2f1a4c12fe5510b2d0798cfdb: C09/batch26-routing-admission-profile/u11a_profile.rs, Git blob 2f38d0e92afb48815ab813b8c887d760b887856d, whole SHA-256 36127a02052ca203cead039dc2dae82e5e77118686ccf1d34c6d6f33bb1a0dda. Before compilation the driver checks the whole bytes/blob and unchanged lines 12–95, block SHA-256 1f927e4d0a780666081a13b4bdc4d2f3ffb94f220ac9bf39cdea8162734e3eb3, then writes an exclusive private include and binds original/generated bytes before and after compilation/execution. This reuses existing published logic; all new extraction/include/verification code counts as authored production. Initial live includes the admitted token; consumed frees remain in signed net delta. Requested traffic, absolute/new phase peak and process VmHWM differ; VmHWM includes admission/setup. summarize.py reports separate seven-sample min/max ranges with raw-input hashes and no pooled p95. The oversized formatted 417-line observer remains immutable pre-reuse provenance, not an executed or accepted implementation.

The independently admitted experimental resource frame uses two CPUs, memory high/max 3/4 GiB, no swap, 128 tasks, fresh host minimum 8 GiB and 660/720-second bounds. It hash-loads the shared ownership helper from #184, attests the actual invocation and controls, and preserves proof-bound cleanup, raw failures and before/after bindings. The inner job owns the nonblocking compiler lock and builds one offline locked release graph with serde_json 1.0.151. verify_routing.py is the exact root-owned 96-line library checker; its original execution/receipt belongs to the separate U11b qualification packet. No source author has executed these new jobs. Native ELK, fractional geometry, connected UI, p95 and successful-capacity acceptance remain OPEN.
